<!--meta {"lead": "The shell is the same on every customer screen: top bar, page header, content, footer. Maya always knows where she is and how to get back.", "description": "App shell, page header, breadcrumbs, tabs vs sub-pages, back behaviour and mobile navigation.", "covers": "Shell, top bar, page header, breadcrumbs, tabs vs sub-pages, back behaviour, mobile menu"} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Every HairPop page uses the same shell: a <a href="../components/skip-link.html">skip link</a>, the sticky <a href="../components/top-bar.html">top bar</a> with Styles, Braiders, Appointments and Help, the account links (Updates with an unread count, Maya), a <a href="../components/page-header.html">page header</a> (eyebrow, h1, subtitle), the content, and the <a href="../components/footer.html">footer</a> with Terms and Privacy. The order and names never change between pages (3.2.3, 3.2.4).</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="when"><h2><a href="#when">When to use which</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Need</th><th scope="col">Use</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Move between the four top-level areas</td><td>Top bar nav links with <code>aria-current="page"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Show where a detail page sits (Styles › Knotless braids › Braiders)</td><td><a href="../components/breadcrumb.html">Breadcrumb</a> above the page header</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Switch views of the same thing without leaving it (Upcoming / Past appointments)</td><td><a href="../components/tabs.html">Tabs</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Content with its own address, worth sharing or bookmarking</td><td>A sub-page with its own URL, not a tab</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Many pages of results</td><td><a href="../components/pagination.html">Pagination</a> under the list</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Settings or help with many sections</td><td><a href="../components/sidebar-navigation.html">Sidebar navigation</a> from 1024px</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="structure"><h2><a href="#structure">Structure</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-frame">
    <header class="topbar"><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a><nav class="topbar__nav" aria-label="Primary"><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" aria-current="page">Styles</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html">Braiders</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/my-appointments/default.html">Appointments</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/help/default.html">Help</a></nav><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon topbar__menu" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false">{{icon:menu}}</button><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/notification-center/default.html" aria-label="Updates, 2 unread">Updates <span class="badge badge--count" aria-hidden="true">2</span></a><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html">Maya</a></header>
    <div class="ds-frame__body">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Styles</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-detail/default.html">Knotless braids</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Braiders</span></li></ol></nav>
      <div class="page-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">Discover</p><p style="font: var(--text-h1); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">Braiders for knotless braids</p><p class="subtitle">12 braiders offer this style near Toronto · prices and availability vary.</p></div></div>
      <p class="text-muted">Content…</p>
    </div>
    <footer class="site-footer"><span>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</span><span><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a> · <a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></span></footer>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <h3>Current, hover and focus</h3>
  {{example:Current page uses the accent tint; hover uses the subtle grey; focus adds the shared ring.}}
<nav aria-label="Navigation states" class="cluster"><a class="nav-link" href="#states" aria-current="page">Styles</a><a class="nav-link" href="#states" data-state="hover">Braiders</a><a class="nav-link" href="#states" data-state="focus">Appointments</a><a class="nav-link" href="#states">Help</a></nav>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Back behaviour</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Browser Back always works: filters and tabs that change the URL push history; transient states (a busy button, a toast, an open dialog) do not.</li>
    <li>Detail pages link back up through the breadcrumb, not a custom "Back" button that guesses the previous page.</li>
    <li>After a success state (request sent), the next step is a forward link ("View request"), and Back returns to the form with its values intact.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes}}<a class="topbar__brand" href="#states">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a><a class="nav-link" href="#states" aria-current="page">Styles</a><a class="nav-link" href="#states">Braiders</a>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>From 768px the four area links sit in the top bar. Below 768px they move into a menu opened by a menu button (<code>.topbar__menu</code>) with <code>aria-expanded</code> and <code>aria-controls</code>; the account links stay visible.</li>
    <li>Breadcrumbs collapse to the parent link only below 768px ("‹ Knotless braids").</li>
    <li>The page header stacks title over actions below 768px; the primary action becomes full width.</li>
    <li>The footer wraps its two groups onto two lines on phones.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Landmarks: <code>header</code>, <code>nav aria-label="Primary"</code>, <code>main id="main"</code>, <code>footer</code>; the skip link is the first focusable element.</li>
    <li>One h1 per page, in the page header; the eyebrow is a paragraph, not a heading.</li>
    <li>The Updates link’s name includes the count ("Updates, 2 unread"); the visual count badge is <code>aria-hidden</code> so it is not read twice.</li>
    <li><code>scroll-padding-top</code> matches the sticky top bar so focused elements are never hidden under it (2.4.11).</li>
    <li>Nav links are 44px tall targets.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Current nav label|--color-fg-accent|--color-accent-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Nav label on top bar|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Brand on top bar|--color-fg-accent|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Area names are single nouns: Styles, Braiders, Appointments, Help.</li>
    <li>Eyebrows group pages: "Discover" for browsing screens, "Your HairPop" for Maya’s own data.</li>
    <li>Page titles speak to Maya: "Find a style that feels like you", "Your appointment with Nia". The <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> puts the specific part first: "Request HP-1048 · HairPop".</li>
    <li>Subtitles carry the key facts in one line, separated by " · ".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false">{{icon:menu}}</button><span class="text-muted">Styles, Braiders, Appointments, Help in a menu</span></div><figcaption>Below 768px, area links move behind a labelled menu button.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="text-muted">Top bar with only the brand and account links</span></div><figcaption>The mocks hide the nav links on phones with no menu, so Styles and Help are unreachable from the bar.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="account-link" href="#do-dont" aria-label="Updates, 2 unread">Updates <span class="badge badge--count" aria-hidden="true">2</span></a></div><figcaption>The count is in the link’s name once.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="account-link" href="#do-dont" aria-label="Notifications, 2 unread">Updates <span class="badge badge--count" aria-label="2 unread">2</span></a></div><figcaption>A label that renames the link ("Notifications" vs visible "Updates", 2.5.3) and a second label on the badge.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|shell, current nav link}}
    {{mock:pages/matching-braiders/default|page header with facts subtitle}}
    {{mock:pages/matching-braiders/long|pagination}}
    {{mock:pages/appointment-detail/default|"Your HairPop" eyebrow}}
    {{mock:pages/help/default|help in the same place}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed: below 768px the mocks hide the area links with no menu button (system adds <code>.topbar__menu</code>); the Updates link was labelled "Notifications, 2 unread", which does not contain its visible text (now "Updates, 2 unread"), and its badge carried a second label (now <code>aria-hidden</code>); the brand mark was a "✦" text glyph (now the sparkle icon); detail pages had no breadcrumb.</p>
</section>
